Package: ethogramR
Type: Package
Title: Behavioural Diversity, Enclosure Use and Social Networks from Scan
    and Focal Data
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R: person("Sitendu", "Goswami", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    email = "sitendugoswami@gmail.com")
Description: Analyses behaviour observations of captive animal groups collected
    by scan (instantaneous) or focal (continuous) sampling, including the
    comma-separated export of the 'Ethogram' observation app. Given an ethogram,
    enclosure zones and the observation records, it calculates activity
    budgets; species-typical behavioural diversity (richness, Shannon-Wiener
    diversity, evenness, Simpson diversity, the share of the repertoire
    expressed and similarity to a wild reference budget) with bootstrap
    confidence intervals, following Miller et al. (2020)
    <doi:10.3390/ani10071211>; the spread of participation index for enclosure
    use with equal zones or unequal zones (Plowman 2003
    <doi:10.1016/S0168-1591(03)00142-4>) and zone electivity; and social
    networks built from simple ratio or half-weight association indices
    (Hoppitt and Farine 2018 <doi:10.1016/j.anbehav.2017.08.029>) or directed
    interaction matrices, with node and network metrics computed with 'igraph'.
    All results are returned as data frames that can be plotted directly with
    'ggplot2'.
